  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Codes stay out of JWTs",
      "items": [
        "6-digit codes are single-use, expire in 24h, and cap wrong guesses; signup is idempotent — re-signup of an unverified email re-issues a code, a verified email answers 409",
        "the verification mail is durable work: an outbox row rides the signup transaction and a BullMQ worker relays the job into Redis",
        "reset codes run 30m with a 3-per-5-minute per-email rate limit; a successful reset auto-verifies and revokes all sessions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Gates",
      "items": [
        "the password verifies first — one constant 401; locked, inactive, and unverified gates run only after, so no probe can infer account state",
        "bcrypt cost 10 over a base64 HMAC-SHA256 pepper pre-hash defeats the 72-byte bcrypt input cap; the pepper lives in env config, never in the DB",
        "zod validates login bodies at the http.ts edge; failures answer the one {detail, code} envelope"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Tokens",
      "items": [
        "access JWT HS256, 15m: sub · email · role · jti — verified by an authx verifier preHandler onto req.identity",
        "the refresh is an opaque token rotated in place under a compare-and-swap on the presented token — a replay mints nothing",
        "change-password revokes other sessions by jti-matched refresh; reset revokes all"
      ]
    }
  ]
}